Article 81: The withdrawal of authorization may be requested by the non-resident financial services provider to the Central Bank of Tunisia, in the case of a provider qualified as a non-resident credit institution, or to the Financial Market Council, in the case of a provider qualified as a non-resident investment firm or non-resident portfolio management company.
The authorization may also be withdrawn on the initiative of the Minister of Finance or on the initiative of the Financial Market Council in cases where:
1) The authorization has not been used within a period of twelve consecutive months from its granting;
2) The provider has ceased its activity for six consecutive months,
3) The provider no longer fulfills the conditions on the basis of which the authorization was granted;
4) The provider obtained the authorization by means of false declarations or any other irregular means;
5) The provider no longer proves that its assets exceed its liabilities towards third parties by an amount equal to the minimum capital or minimum endowment;
6) The causes for a suspension of authorization have not been remedied 6 months after its pronouncement, in the case of non-resident investment firms and non-resident portfolio management companies.

Article 124: Infractions to this Code and its implementing texts shall be prosecuted at the initiative of the Governor of the Central Bank of Tunisia, concerning non-resident credit institutions, and of the College of the Financial Market Council, concerning non-resident investment service providers. These infractions shall expose their perpetrators to one of the following sanctions:
1° a warning;
2° a reprimand;
3° a fine whose amount may reach five times the amount of the infraction concerning non-resident credit institutions, or five times the amount of the profit concerning non-resident investment service providers, without the fine amount being less than the amount of this profit. This fine shall be recovered for the benefit of the General Treasury of Tunisia by means of a liquidation statement issued and made enforceable by the Governor of the Central Bank of Tunisia or the Vice-Governor or the President of the Financial Market Council or their representative. judged necessary, initiated if necessary by the Central Bank of Tunisia or the Financial Market Council.

The decisions of the Financial Services Commission shall be motivated and taken by a majority of the members present. In the event of a tie vote, the President's vote shall be decisive.

The decisions of the Financial Services Commission shall be served by a bailiff.

Article 127: Members of the Financial Services Commission are forbidden to disclose secrets that they have become aware of in the course of their duties, except in cases permitted by law, and under penalty of the sanctions provided for in Article 254 of the Penal Code.

Article 128: Infractions to the provisions of this Code and its implementing texts, complicity in these infractions, or consent to commit them shall expose the members of the Board of Directors, members of the Management Board, members of the Supervisory Board, managers or representatives of non-resident financial service providers, as well as personnel placed under the authority of non-resident investment service providers, members of the Board of Directors, members of the Management Board, members of the Supervisory Board, managers of variable capital investment companies with simplified investment rules and personnel placed under their authority, and personnel placed under the authority of the custodian of expert fund assets, to one of the following sanctions:

