Article 2: For the purposes of this circular, a "complaint" is defined as any statement recording a dispute, dissatisfaction, or objection presented by a customer to an establishment regarding a product or service to which they have subscribed or wish to subscribe, with the exception of domestic mobile payment services governed by Central Bank of Tunisia Circular No. 2020-11 of May 18, 2020.**

**The following are not considered complaints for the purposes of this circular:**
*   A service request;
*   A request for information or advice;
*   A complaint the subject of referral to the banking mediation body or the banking mediator;
*   A complaint that is part of an ongoing case before judicial authorities or the subject of an arbitration procedure;
*   A dispute that has been the subject of a judicial decision or an arbitral award, or that has been the subject of an amicable settlement or a transaction between the customer and the establishment; and
*   A complaint concerning labor relations between the establishment and its employees.

