From the perspective of their operational characteristics, main refinancing operations:
a) Are liquidity-providing operations;
b) Are normally carried out weekly according to the indicative calendar for the regular tender operations of the Central Bank of Tunisia, subject to the exception provided for in paragraph 3;
c) Normally have a maturity of one week, as mentioned in the indicative calendar for the regular tender operations of the Central Bank of Tunisia, subject to the exception provided for in paragraph 3;
d) Are executed by means of tender procedures;
e) Are subject to counterparty eligibility criteria, which must be met by all counterparties submitting bids for these operations;
f) Are based on eligible assets used as collateral.

Article 7

Fine-tuning operations

1. The central bank may conduct fine-tuning operations in the form of repurchase agreements, foreign exchange swaps for monetary policy purposes, or outright liquidity-absorbing operations, on a case-by-case basis in order to manage unforeseen liquidity fluctuations in the market.

2. From the perspective of their operational characteristics, fine-tuning operations:
a) May be conducted in the form of liquidity-providing or liquidity-absorbing operations;
b) Have a frequency that is not standardized;
c) Normally have a maturity shorter than that of main operations;
d) Are normally conducted through tender procedures, unless the central bank decides to carry out the particular fine-tuning operation through a bilateral procedure, taking into account specific monetary policy aspects or in order to react to the market situation;
e) Are subject to counterparty eligibility criteria, which must be met by all counterparties submitting bids for these operations;
