a) May be conducted in the form of liquidity-injecting or liquidity-withdrawing operations;

b) Have a frequency and maturity that are not standardized;

c) Are conducted through auctions or bilateral procedures. 5.

From an operational characteristics perspective, certificates of debt issued by the Central Bank of Tunisia:
a) Are issued as operations initiated by the central bank intended to withdraw liquidity;
b) May be issued on a regular or irregular basis;
